78, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled payments-worker back to v3.3.0 and opened the SEV2. The worker has recovered, but payments-api is still showing errors.\n\n1. **Finding the service:** there's no service called just \"payments\". Two services were unhealthy, both at an 18% error rate: payments-worker on v3.4.0 and payments-api on v5.1.0. You told me the worker was the cause and the API errors come from it.\n2. **Rollback:** payments-worker is back on v3.3.0, its most recent release that was healthy in production, in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It now reports healthy, with errors down from 18% to 0.2%.\n3. **Incident:** SEV2 **INC-0001** is open against payments-worker, and on-call has been paged. My first attempt to create it timed out. The incident list was still empty afterwards, so I retried with the same request ID, which stops a second copy being created. Only one incident exists.\n\n**Still open:** payments-api (v5.1.0) is still unhealthy at 18% errors. It may just need time to recover now that the worker is fixed. I didn't change it because you said its errors come from the worker. If it doesn't recover, its last healthy production release is v5.0.0. I can roll it back to that if you want, but I'd suggest the on-call engineer handling INC-0001 makes that call.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_016SoGMiTR6y9mtLr29zdkjy", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01YLgRKvLK4u5m8Bq49NVqGa", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01Fyuy7ZgLrWwGKetDmjDMV6", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use"